# The driver workspace is REBUILT from bringup/setup_workspace.sh, never committed:
# it contains third-party git checkouts (nested .git), 7 MB of vendored asio headers, and
# build artifacts full of absolute paths that would be wrong on the rover laptop anyway.
ros2_ws/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# symlink into the private sim repo (see config/pipeline/README.md)
config/missions
.last_address
captures/
calib/pairs/

# Map DATA, not map configuration. The .pgm/.yaml pairs and the RViz configs are committed --
# they are small, they are what Nav2 loads, and they are worth reviewing in a diff. These are not:
#   *.posegraph / *.data  slam_toolbox's serialised pose graph, 7-13 MB of binary per map. Only
#                         useful for RESUMING a mapping session on the machine that made it.
#   *_visual/frames/      6-25 MB of recorded frames per run, regenerable from a drive.
# This repo is PUBLIC; 73 MB of binary from one evening's driving does not belong in its history.
maps/*.posegraph
maps/*.data
# Any recorded-frame dump, whatever the run is called. NOTE: gitignore has no inline
# comments -- a trailing '# ...' becomes part of the pattern and silently matches nothing.
maps/*/frames/

# Credentials. Nothing matching these has ever been committed (verified across all 54 commits
# before this repo was made public) and nothing ever should be: the reasoning endpoint's key
# lives in a .env that stays on the machine. See docs/LLM_ENDPOINT.md.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# MOLA 3D maps. Same policy as the slam_toolbox posegraphs above: these are map DATA, they are
# megabytes of binary per drive, and they are regenerable from a drive. Read them back with
#   mm-info -l /opt/ros/jazzy/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libmola_metric_maps.so* <map>.mm
maps/*.mm
maps/*.simplemap
